@startuml state-edit
!include _style.iuml
title The right pane's edits (MainViewModel + ItemDraft)

state "No selection" as None
state "Autosave on" as Auto : EditedItem = the item itself\nevery edit -> LastChange, 500 ms debounced save
state "Draft, clean" as Clean : EditedItem = ItemDraft.Edited (a copy)
state "Draft, dirty" as Dirty : Save button shown
state "Asking" as Asking : "Save changes?" dialog

[*] --> None
None --> Auto : select item [Autosave on]
None --> Clean : select item [Autosave off]\n/ ItemDraft.For(item)
Clean --> Clean : select another item / new draft
Clean --> Dirty : edit differs from the saved item
Dirty --> Clean : edits undone by hand
Dirty --> Clean : Save / Ctrl+S\n/ Commit() + FlushPendingSaveAsync()
Dirty --> Asking : selection leaves the item\n(checked at low priority,\nafter the tree settles)
Asking --> Clean : Save\n/ ResolveSwitchAsync(true), draft of the new item
Asking --> Clean : Don't save\n/ ResolveSwitchAsync(false), draft of the new item
Asking --> Dirty : Cancel\n/ CancelSwitch(), back to the edited item
Dirty --> Dirty : sync refresh replaced the item\n/ RebaseOnto(replacement)
Clean --> Auto : Autosave switched on
Dirty --> Auto : Autosave switched on\n/ SaveEditsAsync()
Auto --> Clean : Autosave switched off

note bottom of Asking
  Closing the window, File > Exit and the tray Exit ask the
  same question (ResolveUnsavedEditsAsync). At Windows
  sign-out nothing can be asked, so the edits are saved.
end note
@enduml
